{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HwiUbdGx29MtxfbuYGa7HA","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 7fb8a9b913f3f9937ce198715a533f5d7f8ad13e\nAuthor: attavo executor (claude-code) <executor+claude-code@attavo.invalid>\nDate:   Fri Sep 25 22:58:59 2026 -0600\n\n    attavo: build #219, the reconciler's R3 -- retries, budgets, ceilings\n    \n    Four retryable families -- died, hung, transient (new: a vendor's\n    capacity, rate, or 5xx refusal, classed on the adapter's own report\n    line), and returned (new: a required check a passed build's head\n    rejected, or a review's own blocking finding) -- retry with no\n    operator, no counsel, inside one shared [drive].attempts budget per\n    stage; a transient waits [drive].retry_after_s first. Every other\n    non-pass record still reaches counsel as before, and an \"answer\"\n    verdict now starts the next attempt steered by it (retry_of and steer\n    on the record); \"patch\" and \"person\" stay the operator's, and a\n    question, a claims-boundary stop, a gate refusal, and an environment\n    refusal are never retried by this item regardless of what counsel\n    rules.\n    \n    Two attempts of one stage ending with the identical stop.signature\n    (a class's own detail or last event, digits stripped) stop the stage\n    early. A stopped, exhausted stage's report carries every attempt's\n    class, signature, bound, wall clock, and cost side by side, whether\n    the last two signatures match, and the rulings available -- --again\n    (retired inside the budget to a no-op that says the pass retries on\n    its own; forces the next attempt, marked again_by, once the budget or\n    the early stop has closed it) and amending the spec.\n    \n    [drive.build].ceiling_s and [drive.verify].ceiling_s bound a stage's\n    wall clock from its own marker; alive past it is hung by the ceiling\n---\ncommit d6154af8c735981fce6993a228ed395b49c24ca4\nAuthor: attavo driver <driver@att